; SPDX-License-Identifier: 0BSD
; naught.source.vla - Naught: Vel et Aut (CART.9), a bench of logic gates: the engine's
; first irregular graph, every gate a formula of the cells it reads. The pass expands this
; file into naught.vla beside it, the rows the engine loads (docs/SPEC.md section 7.8):
; edit this one, then expand it again with
;   cargo run --release --example expand
; Its bench, the block near its end, is written by
;   cargo run --release --example naught
; and never by hand.
;
; The bench. Row 1 names its columns, the switches' letters and the gates' Latin names. A
; 16-bit ripple adder stands from A1, a bit a row from row 3: its switches a and b in
; columns A and B, its carry-in at F2, its five gates a bit in C to G, the sum's bits in G
; and the carry out of its last bit in F18. An 8 by 8 multiplier stands from I1: its
; switches a along row 2 from J2 and b down column I from I4, its partial products in
; J4:Q11, and each of its other roles a block of nine columns to their right, a row of
; carry-save adders a row and its last row the ripple that ends the product. Every cell
; holds 0 or 1, and a 1 is drawn in Lovelace Lavender. Select a switch and type 1 or 0,
; then Enter: the palette opens holding the switch's row,
;   (cell "Bench" "A3" 1)
; Enter writes it, and every gate the switch reaches computes in the act's frame. The
; Lesson, the sheet a load shows first, says the rest to whoever loads it.
;
; The game. Nine levels stand between the Lesson and the Bench, a sheet each, from NON
; built of NON-ET alone to a 4-bit ripple adder (CART.9's third slice): a level's switches,
; the room for a person's gates, its outputs, its lamps, the output due, and its words; T
; tests every input of it, an input a settle step, and its gates are counted against a
; budget and the least known, each read by its formula's text: a gate of a shape outside
; the set the level gives holds a pass to one star. Their keys are the game's, and the
; Bench's are a person's (docs/SPEC.md section 7.2, version 6's (game ...) and (work ...)).
;
; The gates, in Latin, each arithmetic over 0 and 1 and each a macro below:
;   NON, not: 1 less its input.            ET, and: the product of its two.
;   VEL, or: the greater of its two.       AUT, either but not both: their sum's parity.
;   NON-ET, not both: Sheffer's stroke.    NEC, neither: Peirce's arrow.
; Latin is said to keep two ors, vel the inclusive and aut the exclusive. The Stanford
; Encyclopedia of Philosophy's entry of 2016, Ray Jennings and Andrew Hartline's, called
; that a myth in its section 7, and its revision of 2024 says that aut has inclusive uses;
; the bench keeps both anyway.
;
; How it settles. The cartridge says (settle 65536): after an act the engine steps the bench
; again, with no act, until a frame changes nothing (docs/SPEC.md section 5, version 6). At
; full rate every gate a switch reaches computes in the act's own frame, so an act is two
; frames, its own and one that proves nothing moved; the load settles too, so the bench
; opens on its values. The frame floors build their benches without it: a settle numbers
; the Clock by acts, and their switches read the Clock as the frame.
;
; What it measures (docs/REARVIEW.md, CART.9's scoping). A gate reads cells anywhere, so
; the bench is a graph of formulas, its depth the adder's carry rippling through every
; bit. The frame floors build the same bench larger, a 4,096-bit adder and a 64 by 64
; multiplier, twice: laid by fill, each role one shape, and shuffled among the same cells,
; every gate its own shape. What the second costs over the first is the regularity
; premium.

(cartridge "naught"
  (spec 6)                          ; the version of docs/SPEC.md this cartridge is written to: (settle K), (bound ...), (game ...), (read ...) and (work ...)
  (title "Naught: Vel et Aut")      ; what the host shows: the gates' own words
  (rate 0)                          ; an act, an edit or a press, steps the bench; nothing else does
  (screen grid 80 50)               ; no Screen: the host shows the Lesson, the first visible sheet
  (seed 1)                          ; nothing on the bench is drawn from it
  (settle 65536)                    ; an act's settle, at most 65,536 steps: at full rate, one
  (bound "Lesson" "I NON" "II ET" "III VEL" "IV AUT" "V ELIGE" "VI DISTRIBUE" "VII SEMIS" "VIII SUMMA" "IX QUATTUOR" "Bench")  ; the lesson, the levels and the bench, each drawn to its extent and no further
  (read "Lesson")                   ; the lesson, read-only: no key or row of a person's writes it
  (work "Bench")                    ; the bench, a person's to work: every key typed there is a cell's
  (game "I NON" "II ET" "III VEL" "IV AUT" "V ELIGE" "VI DISTRIBUE" "VII SEMIS" "VIII SUMMA" "IX QUATTUOR")  ; the levels: their keys are the game's, T, N, P, R, Space, 1 and 0
  (author "Spreadsheet Company")    ; who wrote it
  (license "0BSD")                  ; the header's twin: copy this file to start a bench of your own
  (notes "Naught: Vel et Aut, a bench of logic gates in Latin: NON, ET, VEL, AUT, NON-ET and NEC. A 16-bit ripple adder from A1 and an 8 by 8 multiplier from I1, every gate a formula of the cells it reads, every 1 in lavender. Select a switch and type 1 or 0, then Enter, (cell \"Bench\" \"A3\" 1), and every gate it reaches computes; the Lesson says the rest."))

; ---- the gates, each a cell or a fill of one formula -----------------------------------
; A gate is written by its Latin name, its cell or its range, then each of its inputs as
; the range's first cell reads it: (aut "C3:C18" "A3" "B3") is the parity of a and b on
; every row from 3 to 18. A gate's value is 0 or 1, a number, so a bus is a sum of its
; bits and a look draws each value. Since KIT.5 each gate is an expression the formula
; syntax writes; an input is the text the generator writes, "A3", made the reference A3 by
; symbol, so the bench's block below stands as its generator wrote it. A gate writes its
; row itself, through formula-expand and never the library's rule, since the frame floors
; build the bench from this source with the lesson, the levels and the include cut out.

(defmacro (non at x)
  "NON, not: 1 less its input"
  (formula "Bench" at (formula-expand (- 1 (symbol x)))))

(defmacro (et at x y)
  "ET, and: the product of its two inputs"
  (formula "Bench" at (formula-expand (* (symbol x) (symbol y)))))

(defmacro (vel at x y)
  "VEL, or: the greater of its two inputs"
  (formula "Bench" at (formula-expand (max (symbol x) (symbol y)))))

(defmacro (aut at x y)
  "AUT, either but not both: the parity of its inputs' sum"
  (formula "Bench" at (formula-expand (mod (+ (symbol x) (symbol y)) 2))))

(defmacro (non-et at x y)
  "NON-ET, not both, Sheffer's stroke: 1 less the product of its inputs"
  (formula "Bench" at (formula-expand (- 1 (* (symbol x) (symbol y))))))

(defmacro (nec at x y)
  "NEC, neither, Peirce's arrow: 1 less the greater of its inputs"
  (formula "Bench" at (formula-expand (- 1 (max (symbol x) (symbol y))))))

; A command's test and a level's number, named once for the levels and the Lab.
(defmacro (a-command word)
  "the command named by the word, run at this frame: Input!$B$20=\"word\""
  (= Input!$B$20 word))

(defmacro (shown-as level k)
  "a level's number where it is the sheet shown, and 0 otherwise: (Input!$B$19=\"level\")*k"
  (* (= Input!$B$19 level) k))

; ---- the lesson beside the bench: the floors build their benches without it ----
; What the game teaches, on a sheet of its own, the first a load shows, bound to its extent and read-only: a line a row
; in a column wide enough to hold it. Its own sheet keeps the Bench's cells numbers alone, which the language reads as
; arrays.
(sheet "Lesson" visible)
(column "Lesson" "A" 140 shown none)
(cell "Lesson" "A1" "Naught: Vel et Aut")
(cell "Lesson" "A2" "Logic gates in Latin, and nine levels that build them from one: NON, ET, VEL and AUT, a choice, a send, two sums and four bits.")
(cell "Lesson" "A3" "The levels are the sheets after this one: a tab, or Ctrl+Alt+PageDown (Ctrl+PageDown in full screen), and Ctrl+Alt+PageUp back.")
(cell "Lesson" "A5" "On a level, Space toggles the switch the selection stands on, 1 and 0 set it, a click toggles it. A lamp is lit where its output is 1.")
(cell "Lesson" "A6" "Write the gates in the room, C to I, and the outputs in J: type = on a cell, and the palette opens its formula. Enter writes it.")
(cell "Lesson" "A7" "Enter on a cell opens its formula as it stands, F2 too, and Escape leaves it. Delete empties a cell; Tab moves right.")
(cell "Lesson" "A8" "T tests every input, an input a frame, and stops at the first a lamp gets wrong, the board standing on it. R sets the switches to 0.")
(cell "Lesson" "A9" "N and P show the next and the previous level. A pass is a star; within the budget, two; at the least known, three, until the next test.")
(cell "Lesson" "A11" "The gates, in Latin: NON, not, =1-a. ET, and, =a*b. VEL, or, =MAX(a,b). AUT, either but not both, =MOD(a+b,2).")
(cell "Lesson" "A12" "NON-ET, not both, =1-a*b, Sheffer's stroke. NEC, neither, =1-MAX(a,b), Peirce's arrow. Either alone builds every other gate.")
(cell "Lesson" "A13" "Level I gives NON-ET alone; each later level, the gates proven before it, and a wire, =a. Any other shape caps a pass at one star.")
(cell "Lesson" "A14" "A gate reads the switches, the room's cells, 0 or 1. The reckoning names the first gate outside the set; the verdict, an error's cell.")
(cell "Lesson" "A15" "After the levels, the Bench, a sandbox where every key types: a 16-bit adder from A1 and an 8 by 8 multiplier from I1.")
(cell "Lesson" "A16" "The adder: a in A3:A18 and b in B3:B18, low bit first, its carry-in F2; its sum G3:G18, its carry out F18.")
(cell "Lesson" "A17" "Each bit adds three: C = AUT(a,b), D = ET(a,b), E = ET(C,carry), F = VEL(D,E) the carry on, G = AUT(C,carry) the sum.")
(cell "Lesson" "A18" "The multiplier: a in J2:Q2 and b in I4:I11, low bit first; its partial products ET(a,b) in J4:Q11, summed in rows.")
(cell "Lesson" "A19" "Its product, low bit first: J4, S5, BC6:BC11, S12, BD12:BI12 and AZ12.")
(cell "Lesson" "A20" "Try it: a all ones, A3:A18, then the carry-in F2 to 1: 65,535 + 1 ripples through all sixteen bits in one act. 255 x 255 = 65,025.")
(cell "Lesson" "A21" "Delete empties a cell, Backspace opens it emptied: an empty text is no number, so the gates it feeds say #VALUE!. Ex nihilo nihil fit.")
(cell "Lesson" "A23" "Tertium non datur: a cell holds 0 or 1, and no third, Delete aside. Latin is said to keep two ors, vel and aut; the Stanford")
(cell "Lesson" "A24" "Encyclopedia of Philosophy called that a myth in 2016: aut has inclusive uses too. Naught keeps both anyway.")
; ---- the lesson's end ----

; ---- the levels: the game, between the lesson and the bench; the floors build their benches without them ----
; A level a sheet (CART.9's third slice, decisions 16 to 28), bound to its extent: its title in row 1 and its heads in
; row 2; its switches in column A from row 3, each named beside it in B; the room for its gates, C to I, and its outputs
; in J, each named in K, which a person writes as formulas, = opening a cell's edit; a lamp a row in L, lit while its
; output is 1; the output due in M, the specification's at the switches standing; and its words in N, its reckoning
; and its test's verdict in N8 and N9. Its keys are the game's, the manifest's (game ...): Space toggles the switch the
; selection stands on, 1 and 0 set it, and a click toggles it; T tests every input; R sets the switches to 0; N and P
; show the next and the previous level. The Lab keeps the test and each level's reckoning, the Gates sheet reads each
; gate of its room by its formula's text, the Camera shows the level N and P move to, and the Commands sheet holds the
; keys.
(include "../common.vla")

(format 2 "A080E0" general nowrap)  ; a lamp lit, the lamps' lavender

(defmacro (level-sheet sheet)
  "a level's sheet: its columns, a 1 lit in the gates' lavender and a lamp lit in the lamps'"
  (column sheet "A" 4 shown none)
  (column sheet "B" 3 shown none)
  (column sheet "C" 4 shown none)
  (column sheet "D" 4 shown none)
  (column sheet "E" 4 shown none)
  (column sheet "F" 4 shown none)
  (column sheet "G" 4 shown none)
  (column sheet "H" 4 shown none)
  (column sheet "I" 4 shown none)
  (column sheet "J" 4 shown none)
  (column sheet "K" 6 shown none)
  (column sheet "L" 5 shown none)
  (column sheet "M" 4 shown none)
  (column sheet "N" 128 shown none)
  (look sheet 1 1)
  (look sheet "●" 2))

(defmacro (level-heads sheet title)
  "a level's title in A1, over the empty row to its right, and its columns' heads in row 2"
  (cell sheet "A1" title)
  (cell sheet "A2" "in")
  (cell sheet "C2" "the room")
  (cell sheet "J2" "out")
  (cell sheet "L2" "lamp")
  (cell sheet "M2" "due"))

(defmacro (level-switches sheet lab-row range)
  "a level's switches, each its own last value: 0 at R on its level; while T runs its level, the bit of the input's number
   that the switch's row names; and otherwise Space, 1, 0 or a click on it. lab-row, the level's row of the Lab"
  (rule sheet range
    (if (and (a-command "reset") (= Input!$B$19 sheet)) 0                                        ; R on the level: 0
      (if (= (ref "Lab" (&expand "$N$" lab-row)) 1)                                               ; T running the level:
          (mod (int (/ Lab!$B$6 (choose (- (row) 2) 1 2 4 8 16 32 64 128 256))) 2)                ;   the bit of the input's number its row names
          (if (and (= Input!$B$19 sheet) (= Input!$B$11 1) (= Input!$B$12 (row)))                 ; an act on the switch:
              (if (a-command "one") 1                                                             ;   1, 0,
                (if (a-command "zero") 0
                  (if (or (a-command "toggle") (= Input!$B$13 1)) (- 1 (ref (&expand sheet ".last") "A3"))   ;   or toggled by Space or a click;
                      (ref (&expand sheet ".last") "A3"))))
              (ref (&expand sheet ".last") "A3"))))))                                             ; else as it was

(defmacro (level-lamps sheet range)
  "a level's lamps, a dot lit in the lamps' lavender while the output to its left is 1, a ring otherwise, and a question
   mark while it holds an error, which is neither"
  (rule sheet range (iferror (if (= J3 1) "●" "○") "?")))

(defmacro (level-reckoning sheet lab-row inputs budget least)
  "a level's reckoning in N8: its gates, how many stand outside the set it gives and the first of them, its budget and
   the least known, and its last test's stars; and its test's verdict in N9, counting the inputs while T runs, and
   naming the room's first cell that holds an error. lab-row, the level's row of the Lab"
  (rule sheet "N8"
    (& "Gates " (ref "Lab" (&expand "E" lab-row))
       (if (> (ref "Lab" (&expand "Q" lab-row)) 0)
           (& ", " (ref "Lab" (&expand "Q" lab-row)) " outside the set given, the first at " (ref "Lab" (&expand "R" lab-row)))
           "")
       (&expand "; the budget " budget ", the least known " least ": ") (ref "Lab" (&expand "H" lab-row))))
  (rule sheet "N9"
    (if (= (ref "Lab" (&expand "N" lab-row)) 1) (& "Calculemus: input " (+ Lab!$B$6 1) (&expand " of " inputs))
      (if (= (ref "Lab" (&expand "B" lab-row)) 2)
          (& "The test stops at input " (+ (ref "Lab" (&expand "C" lab-row)) 1) (&expand " of " inputs ", standing on the board: ")
             (if (= (ref "Lab" (&expand "S" lab-row)) "")
                 "a lamp differs from its due."
                 (& (ref "Lab" (&expand "S" lab-row)) " holds an error: it reads a text, an emptied cell or an error.")))
        (if (<> (ref "Lab" (&expand "S" lab-row)) "")
            (& (ref "Lab" (&expand "S" lab-row)) " holds an error: it reads a text, an emptied cell or an error. Ex nihilo nihil fit.")
          (if (= (ref "Lab" (&expand "B" lab-row)) 1)
              (&expand "Quod erat demonstrandum: every one of its " inputs " inputs passes.")
              "T tests every input, an input a frame. Calculemus!"))))))

(defmacro (level-keys sheet at)
  "the keys of a level, said where it has room; and below its verdict, in N10, what a write over the cartridge's own cells
   costs (decision 23): a formula enters by the load or a person's write, and R writes values"
  (cell sheet at "Space toggles the switch the selection stands on, 1 and 0 set it, a click toggles it; T tests, R resets, N and P move.")
  (cell sheet "N10" "A switch or a lamp written over is lost until Load, which loads every level afresh: R writes values, never a formula."))

; ---- I NON: not, from NON-ET alone ----
(sheet "I NON" visible)
(level-sheet "I NON")
(level-heads "I NON" "I NON: not, from NON-ET alone")
(cells "I NON" ("B3" "a") ("K3" "y"))
(level-switches "I NON" 11 "A3")
(level-lamps "I NON" "L3")
(rules "I NON" ("M3" Lab!I11))
(cells "I NON"
  ("N1" "NON, not: the lamp lit where a is 0, and dark where a is 1.")
  ("N2" "Given NON-ET alone, not both, =1-x*y. Write y in J3, with any gates before it in the room, C to I.")
  ("N3" "A gate's two inputs may be one cell read twice.")
  ("N4" "NON-ET alone builds every gate: Peirce found it about 1880 and never published it, and Sheffer did, in 1913.")
  ("N5" "Tertium non datur: a lamp is lit or it is dark, and there is no third.")
  ("N6" "Ockham's razor, in words found in none of Ockham's extant works: entities are not to be multiplied beyond necessity."))
(level-keys "I NON" "N7")
(level-reckoning "I NON" 11 2 2 1)

; ---- II ET: and, from NON-ET and NON ----
(sheet "II ET" visible)
(level-sheet "II ET")
(level-heads "II ET" "II ET: and, from NON-ET and NON")
(cells "II ET" ("B3" "a") ("B4" "b") ("K3" "y"))
(level-switches "II ET" 12 "A3:A4")
(level-lamps "II ET" "L3")
(rules "II ET" ("M3" Lab!I12))
(cells "II ET"
  ("N1" "ET, and: the lamp lit where a and b are both 1.")
  ("N2" "Given NON-ET, =1-x*y, and NON, proven at I, =1-x. Write y in J3.")
  ("N3" "De Morgan, 1847: not both is the one not or the other not, NON-ET(a,b) = VEL(NON a, NON b). Turn it around."))
(level-keys "II ET" "N7")
(level-reckoning "II ET" 12 4 3 2)

; ---- III VEL: or, the inclusive ----
(sheet "III VEL" visible)
(level-sheet "III VEL")
(level-heads "III VEL" "III VEL: or, the inclusive")
(cells "III VEL" ("B3" "a") ("B4" "b") ("K3" "y"))
(level-switches "III VEL" 13 "A3:A4")
(level-lamps "III VEL" "L3")
(rules "III VEL" ("M3" Lab!I13))
(cells "III VEL"
  ("N1" "VEL, or: the lamp lit where a or b is 1, or both.")
  ("N2" "Given NON-ET, =1-x*y; NON, =1-x; and ET, proven at II, =x*y. Write y in J3.")
  ("N3" "Chrysippus's dog, at a fork of three roads, sniffs two, finds no scent, and takes the third unsniffed.")
  ("N4" "It reasoned in VEL: this road or that or the other, not this, not that, so the other."))
(level-keys "III VEL" "N7")
(level-reckoning "III VEL" 13 4 4 3)

; ---- IV AUT: either, but not both ----
(sheet "IV AUT" visible)
(level-sheet "IV AUT")
(level-heads "IV AUT" "IV AUT: either, but not both")
(cells "IV AUT" ("B3" "a") ("B4" "b") ("K3" "y"))
(level-switches "IV AUT" 14 "A3:A4")
(level-lamps "IV AUT" "L3")
(rules "IV AUT" ("M3" Lab!I14))
(cells "IV AUT"
  ("N1" "AUT, either but not both: the lamp lit where exactly one of a and b is 1.")
  ("N2" "Given NON-ET, NON, ET, and VEL, proven at III, =MAX(x,y). Write y in J3.")
  ("N3" "Latin is said to keep two ors, vel the inclusive and aut the exclusive; the Stanford Encyclopedia called that a myth in 2016.")
  ("N4" "Aut has inclusive uses too. Here it is exclusive anyway, and VEL and NON-ET together nearly say it."))
(level-keys "IV AUT" "N7")
(level-reckoning "IV AUT" 14 4 5 3)

; ---- V ELIGE: choose, a multiplexer ----
(sheet "V ELIGE" visible)
(level-sheet "V ELIGE")
(level-heads "V ELIGE" "V ELIGE: choose, a multiplexer")
(cells "V ELIGE" ("B3" "a") ("B4" "b") ("B5" "s") ("K3" "y"))
(level-switches "V ELIGE" 15 "A3:A5")
(level-lamps "V ELIGE" "L3")
(rules "V ELIGE" ("M3" Lab!I15))
(cells "V ELIGE"
  ("N1" "ELIGE, choose: y is a where s is 0, and b where s is 1.")
  ("N2" "Given every gate proven, NON, ET, VEL and AUT, beside NON-ET. Write y in J3.")
  ("N3" "A choice made by a wire: s decides which input the lamp follows, and nothing else."))
(level-keys "V ELIGE" "N7")
(level-reckoning "V ELIGE" 15 8 5 3)

; ---- VI DISTRIBUE: send, a demultiplexer ----
(sheet "VI DISTRIBUE" visible)
(level-sheet "VI DISTRIBUE")
(level-heads "VI DISTRIBUE" "VI DISTRIBUE: send, a demultiplexer")
(cells "VI DISTRIBUE" ("B3" "x") ("B4" "s") ("K3" "to 0") ("K4" "to 1"))
(level-switches "VI DISTRIBUE" 16 "A3:A4")
(level-lamps "VI DISTRIBUE" "L3:L4")
(rules "VI DISTRIBUE" ("M3" Lab!I16) ("M4" Lab!J16))
(cells "VI DISTRIBUE"
  ("N1" "DISTRIBUE, send: x goes to J3 where s is 0, and to J4 where s is 1, the other output 0.")
  ("N2" "Given every gate proven. Write J3 and J4.")
  ("N3" "The wire chooses again: where, now, and not which."))
(level-keys "VI DISTRIBUE" "N7")
(level-reckoning "VI DISTRIBUE" 16 4 4 2)

; ---- VII SEMIS: the half, a half adder ----
(sheet "VII SEMIS" visible)
(level-sheet "VII SEMIS")
(level-heads "VII SEMIS" "VII SEMIS: the half, a half adder")
(cells "VII SEMIS" ("B3" "a") ("B4" "b") ("K3" "sum") ("K4" "carry"))
(level-switches "VII SEMIS" 17 "A3:A4")
(level-lamps "VII SEMIS" "L3:L4")
(rules "VII SEMIS" ("M3" Lab!I17) ("M4" Lab!J17))
(cells "VII SEMIS"
  ("N1" "SEMIS, the half: a + b in two bits, the sum in J3 and the carry in J4; 1 + 1 is the sum 0 and the carry 1.")
  ("N2" "Given every gate proven.")
  ("N3" "Calculemus, said Leibniz: let us calculate, and a dispute is settled. Here a sum is two gates."))
(level-keys "VII SEMIS" "N7")
(level-reckoning "VII SEMIS" 17 4 3 2)

; ---- VIII SUMMA: the whole sum, a full adder ----
(sheet "VIII SUMMA" visible)
(level-sheet "VIII SUMMA")
(level-heads "VIII SUMMA" "VIII SUMMA: the whole sum, a full adder")
(cells "VIII SUMMA" ("B3" "a") ("B4" "b") ("B5" "c") ("K3" "sum") ("K4" "carry"))
(level-switches "VIII SUMMA" 18 "A3:A5")
(level-lamps "VIII SUMMA" "L3:L4")
(rules "VIII SUMMA" ("M3" Lab!I18) ("M4" Lab!J18))
(cells "VIII SUMMA"
  ("N1" "SUMMA, the whole sum: a + b + c in two bits, the sum in J3 and the carry in J4, c the carry coming in.")
  ("N2" "Given every gate proven, and the half adder's idea.")
  ("N3" "Calculemus: two halves and an or make a whole, and the carry moves on."))
(level-keys "VIII SUMMA" "N7")
(level-reckoning "VIII SUMMA" 18 8 6 5)

; ---- IX QUATTUOR: four bits, a ripple adder ----
(sheet "IX QUATTUOR" visible)
(level-sheet "IX QUATTUOR")
(level-heads "IX QUATTUOR" "IX QUATTUOR: four bits, a ripple adder")
(cells "IX QUATTUOR"
  ("B3" "a0") ("B4" "a1") ("B5" "a2") ("B6" "a3") ("B7" "b0") ("B8" "b1") ("B9" "b2") ("B10" "b3") ("B11" "c")
  ("K3" "s0") ("K4" "s1") ("K5" "s2") ("K6" "s3") ("K7" "carry"))
(level-switches "IX QUATTUOR" 19 "A3:A11")
(level-lamps "IX QUATTUOR" "L3:L7")
(rules "IX QUATTUOR" ("M3" Lab!I19) ("M4" Lab!J19) ("M5" Lab!K19) ("M6" Lab!L19) ("M7" Lab!M19))
(cells "IX QUATTUOR"
  ("N1" "QUATTUOR, four: a in A3:A6, plus b in A7:A10, plus the carry c in A11, low bit first; the sum in J3:J6, its carry in J7.")
  ("N2" "Given every gate proven, and the whole sum's idea four times over.")
  ("N3" "The carry ripples from bit to bit: 15 + 1 runs it through all four. T tries all 512 inputs, an input a frame.")
  ("N4" "The Liar: a gate that reads itself says this sentence is false, and the language refuses its write, naming its cells."))
(level-keys "IX QUATTUOR" "N7")
(level-reckoning "IX QUATTUOR" 19 512 21 20)

; ---- the Lab: the level N and P show, the test, and each level's reckoning ----
; B1 the level the act stands on, 1 to 9, or 0 off the levels; B2 the level N and P move to, from the level shown, and
; B3 its sheet for the Camera at their act alone, the empty text between, so that a person's tabs win; B4 the level
; under test and B5 whether its test runs; B6 the input shown, its number, whose bits the switches take while the test
; runs, and B7 the inputs there are; B8 whether every output is due at this frame. T begins a test at input 0, and it
; goes on a settle step an input while every lamp is due, standing at the first input that fails or at the last.
(sheet "Lab" hidden)
(labels "Lab" "A1" "shown" "level" "camera" "testing" "running" "input" "inputs" "due")
(rules "Lab"
  ("B1" (+ (shown-as "I NON" 1) (shown-as "II ET" 2) (shown-as "III VEL" 3) (shown-as "IV AUT" 4) (shown-as "V ELIGE" 5) (shown-as "VI DISTRIBUE" 6) (shown-as "VII SEMIS" 7) (shown-as "VIII SUMMA" 8) (shown-as "IX QUATTUOR" 9)))
  ("B2" (if (and (a-command "next") (> B1 0)) (min 9 (+ B1 1)) (if (and (a-command "previous") (> B1 0)) (max 1 (- B1 1)) (max 1 Lab.last!B2))))
  ("B3" (if (or (a-command "next") (a-command "previous")) (choose B2 "I NON" "II ET" "III VEL" "IV AUT" "V ELIGE" "VI DISTRIBUE" "VII SEMIS" "VIII SUMMA" "IX QUATTUOR") ""))
  ("B4" (if (a-command "test") B1 Lab.last!B4))
  ("B5" (if (a-command "test") (if (> B1 0) 1 0) (if (a-command "reset") 0 (if (= Lab.last!B5 1) (if (and (= Lab.last!B8 1) (< Lab.last!B6 (- Lab.last!B7 1))) 1 0) 0))))
  ("B6" (if (a-command "test") 0 (if (and (= Lab.last!B5 1) (= B5 1)) (+ Lab.last!B6 1) Lab.last!B6)))
  ("B7" (choose (max 1 B4) 2 4 4 4 8 4 4 8 512))
  ("B8" (choose (max 1 B4) D11 D12 D13 D14 D15 D16 D17 D18 D19)))
; Rows 11 to 19, a level a row: B the last test's result, 0 none, 1 passed and 2 failed, R on the level forgetting it; C
; the input it stopped at; D whether every output is due now, an error never; E its gates, every formula of its room; F
; its budget and G the least known; H its stars, its last test's; I to M its outputs due, the specification's at its
; inputs as its test reads them, rows 21 on; N whether its test runs; O, IX's, the sum a + b + c; P the inputs a gate of
; it may read, between bars; Q its gates outside the set it gives, R the first of them and S the room's first cell
; holding an error, each read row by row; and T and U its gates and those outside when its test last ended.
(labels "Lab" "A11" "I NON" "II ET" "III VEL" "IV AUT" "V ELIGE" "VI DISTRIBUE" "VII SEMIS" "VIII SUMMA" "IX QUATTUOR")
(headers "Lab" "B10" "result" "stopped at" "due" "gates" "budget" "least" "stars" "due 0" "due 1" "due 2" "due 3" "due 4" "testing" "sum"
  "inputs" "outside" "first outside" "first error" "gates tested" "outside tested")

(defmacro (lab-level r k budget least)
  "a level's row of the Lab, r its row and k its number: its result, the input its test stopped at, its budget, its least
   known, its gates and those outside the set when its test last ended, its stars, and whether its test runs. A result,
   its input and its gates change only while the level is under test, so a test's stars are its own: a gate written or
   emptied after it moves none until T or R"
  (rule "Lab" (&expand "B" r)
    (if (and (a-command "reset") (= $B$1 k)) 0                                                   ; R on the level forgets its test;
      (if (or (<> Lab.last!$B$4 k) (<> $B$4 k)) (ref "Lab.last" (&expand "B" r))                  ; another level under test: as it was;
        (if (and (= Lab.last!$B$5 1) (= $B$5 0)) (if (= Lab.last!$B$8 1) 1 2)                   ; the test just ended: passed, or failed,
            (ref "Lab.last" (&expand "B" r))))))                                                   ; else as it was
  (rule "Lab" (&expand "C" r)
    (if (or (<> Lab.last!$B$4 k) (<> $B$4 k)) (ref "Lab.last" (&expand "C" r))
      (if (and (= Lab.last!$B$5 1) (= $B$5 0)) Lab.last!$B$6 (ref "Lab.last" (&expand "C" r)))))
  (cell "Lab" (&expand "F" r) budget)
  (cell "Lab" (&expand "G" r) least)
  (rule "Lab" (&expand "T" r)
    (if (or (<> Lab.last!$B$4 k) (<> $B$4 k)) (ref "Lab.last" (&expand "T" r))
      (if (and (= Lab.last!$B$5 1) (= $B$5 0)) (symbol "E" r) (ref "Lab.last" (&expand "T" r)))))
  (rule "Lab" (&expand "U" r)
    (if (or (<> Lab.last!$B$4 k) (<> $B$4 k)) (ref "Lab.last" (&expand "U" r))
      (if (and (= Lab.last!$B$5 1) (= $B$5 0)) (symbol "Q" r) (ref "Lab.last" (&expand "U" r)))))
  (rule "Lab" (&expand "H" r)                                                                      ; a gate outside: one star
    (if (= (symbol "B" r) 1)
        (if (> (symbol "U" r) 0) "★☆☆" (if (<= (symbol "T" r) (symbol "G" r)) "★★★" (if (<= (symbol "T" r) (symbol "F" r)) "★★☆" "★☆☆")))
        "☆☆☆"))
  (rule "Lab" (&expand "N" r) (if (= $B$4 k) $B$5 0)))

(defmacro (lab-inputs sheet lab-row range)
  "a level's inputs as its test reads them, down its column of the Lab from row 21: while T runs the level, the bits of
   the input's number, which its switches take; and otherwise its switches as they stand. A switch a person wrote over
   stands still (decision 23), so the due under test is the specification at the input, never at a switch that does not
   move. lab-row, the level's row of the Lab"
  (rule "Lab" range
    (if (= (symbol "$N$" lab-row) 1) (mod (int (/ $B$6 (choose (- (row) 20) 1 2 4 8 16 32 64 128 256))) 2) (ref sheet "A3"))))

(lab-level 11 1 2 1)
(lab-level 12 2 3 2)
(lab-level 13 3 4 3)
(lab-level 14 4 5 3)
(lab-level 15 5 5 3)
(lab-level 16 6 4 2)
(lab-level 17 7 3 2)
(lab-level 18 8 6 5)
(lab-level 19 9 21 20)
; Rows 21 on, a level a column, B for I to J for IX: its inputs as its test reads them, input 0 in row 21
(labels "Lab" "A21" "input 0" "input 1" "input 2" "input 3" "input 4" "input 5" "input 6" "input 7" "input 8")
(headers "Lab" "B20" "I NON" "II ET" "III VEL" "IV AUT" "V ELIGE" "VI DISTRIBUE" "VII SEMIS" "VIII SUMMA" "IX QUATTUOR")
(lab-inputs "I NON" 11 "B21")
(lab-inputs "II ET" 12 "C21:C22")
(lab-inputs "III VEL" 13 "D21:D22")
(lab-inputs "IV AUT" 14 "E21:E22")
(lab-inputs "V ELIGE" 15 "F21:F23")
(lab-inputs "VI DISTRIBUE" 16 "G21:G22")
(lab-inputs "VII SEMIS" 17 "H21:H22")
(lab-inputs "VIII SUMMA" 18 "I21:I23")
(lab-inputs "IX QUATTUOR" 19 "J21:J29")
; each level's specification at its inputs as its test reads them, and whether every output is due, an output holding an
; error never: the test stops there, and the verdict names the error's cell
(defmacro (output level cell)
  "a level's output, a reference into its sheet, whose name needs quotes"
  (ref level cell))
(rules "Lab"
  ("I11" (- 1 B21))
  ("D11" (iferror (if (= (output "I NON" "J3") I11) 1 0) 0))
  ("I12" (* C21 C22))
  ("D12" (iferror (if (= (output "II ET" "J3") I12) 1 0) 0))
  ("I13" (max D21 D22))
  ("D13" (iferror (if (= (output "III VEL" "J3") I13) 1 0) 0))
  ("I14" (mod (+ E21 E22) 2))
  ("D14" (iferror (if (= (output "IV AUT" "J3") I14) 1 0) 0))
  ("I15" (if (= F23 1) F22 F21))
  ("D15" (iferror (if (= (output "V ELIGE" "J3") I15) 1 0) 0))
  ("I16" (* G21 (- 1 G22)))
  ("J16" (* G21 G22))
  ("D16" (iferror (if (and (= (output "VI DISTRIBUE" "J3") I16) (= (output "VI DISTRIBUE" "J4") J16)) 1 0) 0))
  ("I17" (mod (+ H21 H22) 2))
  ("J17" (int (/ (+ H21 H22) 2)))
  ("D17" (iferror (if (and (= (output "VII SEMIS" "J3") I17) (= (output "VII SEMIS" "J4") J17)) 1 0) 0))
  ("I18" (mod (+ I21 I22 I23) 2))
  ("J18" (int (/ (+ I21 I22 I23) 2)))
  ("D18" (iferror (if (and (= (output "VIII SUMMA" "J3") I18) (= (output "VIII SUMMA" "J4") J18)) 1 0) 0))
  ("O19" (+ J21 (* 2 J22) (* 4 J23) (* 8 J24) J25 (* 2 J26) (* 4 J27) (* 8 J28) J29))
  ("I19" (mod O19 2))
  ("J19" (mod (int (/ O19 2)) 2))
  ("K19" (mod (int (/ O19 4)) 2))
  ("L19" (mod (int (/ O19 8)) 2))
  ("M19" (int (/ O19 16)))
  ("D19" (iferror (if (and (= (output "IX QUATTUOR" "J3") I19) (= (output "IX QUATTUOR" "J4") J19) (= (output "IX QUATTUOR" "J5") K19) (= (output "IX QUATTUOR" "J6") L19) (= (output "IX QUATTUOR" "J7") M19)) 1 0) 0)))
; ---- the Gates: each level's room read by its formulas' texts (CART.9's short slice of 2026-10-24) ----
; A gate is a formula of the room, C3 to J at the board's last row, 10 or IX's 11 (ISFORMULA), so a value is none; and
; each is read by its text (FORMULATEXT), its spaces and its $ gone and upper-cased, as one of the set a level gives:
; a wire =x, NON-ET =1-x*y, NON =1-x, ET =x*y, VEL =MAX(x,y) or AUT =MOD(x+y,2), each input a switch of the level, a
; cell of its room, 0 or 1. Any other formula is outside the set, as a gate the level does not give yet is. A block a
; level, 20 rows apart from row 3: the texts in C to J, and the kinds ten columns to their right.
(defmacro (among-inputs x ops)
  "an input a level's gate may read: its text, between bars, among the level's inputs, ops"
  (not (iserror (find (& "|" x "|") ops))))

(defmacro (gate-kind f ops)
  "a cell's kind by its formula's text f, spaces and $ gone and upper-cased, ops the level's inputs between bars: 0 no
   formula; 1 a wire, =x; 2 NON-ET, =1-x*y; 3 NON, =1-x; 4 ET, =x*y; 5 VEL, =MAX(x,y); 6 AUT, =MOD(x+y,2); and 9 any
   other formula. A shape's inputs found by its marks, so an input holding any other mark is no input"
  (if (= f "") 0
    (if (among-inputs (mid f 2 99) ops) 1
      (if (and (= (left f 3) "=1-") (iferror (and (among-inputs (mid f 4 (- (find "*" f) 4)) ops) (among-inputs (mid f (+ (find "*" f) 1) 99) ops)) false)) 2
        (if (and (= (left f 3) "=1-") (among-inputs (mid f 4 99) ops)) 3
          (if (iferror (and (among-inputs (mid f 2 (- (find "*" f) 2)) ops) (among-inputs (mid f (+ (find "*" f) 1) 99) ops)) false) 4
            (if (and (= (left f 5) "=MAX(") (= (right f 1) ")") (iferror (and (among-inputs (mid f 6 (- (find "," f) 6)) ops) (among-inputs (mid f (+ (find "," f) 1) (- (len f) (find "," f) 1)) ops)) false)) 5
              (if (and (= (left f 5) "=MOD(") (= (right f 3) ",2)") (iferror (and (among-inputs (mid f 6 (- (find "+" f) 6)) ops) (among-inputs (mid f (+ (find "+" f) 1) (- (len f) (find "+" f) 3)) ops)) false)) 6
                9))))))))

(defmacro (room-address i)
  "the address of a room's cell by its place i in the room read row by row from C3, eight cells a row"
  (& (mid "CDEFGHIJ" (+ (mod (- i 1) 8) 1) 1) (+ 3 (int (/ (- i 1) 8)))))

(defmacro (lab-gates sheet r top rows switches gives)
  "a level's gates read from their formulas: on the Gates sheet, its block from row top, each room cell's text and its
   kind; and on its row r of the Lab, its gates, every formula of its room (E), the inputs a gate may read (P), its gates
   outside the set it gives, kinds past gives (Q), the first of them (R), and the room's first cell holding an error (S).
   rows, its room's rows from 3; switches, its switches"
  (rule "Gates" (&expand "C" top ":J" (+expand top (-expand rows 1)))
    (iferror (upper (substitute (substitute (formulatext (ref sheet "C3")) " " "") "$" "")) ""))
  (rule "Gates" (&expand "M" top ":T" (+expand top (-expand rows 1)))
    (gate-kind (symbol "C" top) (symbol "Lab!$P$" r)))
  (rule "Lab" (&expand "E" r) (sumproduct (- (- (isformula (ref sheet (&expand "C3:J" (+expand rows 2))))))))
  (rule "Lab" (&expand "P" r)
    (& "|" (textjoin "|" true (& "A" (sequence switches 1 3)) (& (mid "CDEFGHIJ" (sequence 1 8) 1) (sequence rows 1 3)) "0" "1") "|"))
  (rule "Lab" (&expand "Q" r) (countif (ref "Gates" (&expand "M" top ":T" (+expand top (-expand rows 1)))) (&expand ">" gives)))
  (rule "Lab" (&expand "R" r)
    (iferror (room-address (match true (> (tocol (ref "Gates" (&expand "M" top ":T" (+expand top (-expand rows 1))))) gives) 0)) ""))
  (rule "Lab" (&expand "S" r)
    (iferror (room-address (match true (iserror (tocol (ref sheet (&expand "C3:J" (+expand rows 2))))) 0)) "")))

(sheet "Gates" hidden)
(cells "Gates"
  ("C1" "each room cell's formula, spaces and $ gone and upper-cased")
  ("M1" "its kind: 0 none, 1 a wire, 2 NON-ET, 3 NON, 4 ET, 5 VEL, 6 AUT, 9 outside the set")
  ("A3" "I NON") ("A23" "II ET") ("A43" "III VEL") ("A63" "IV AUT") ("A83" "V ELIGE") ("A103" "VI DISTRIBUE")
  ("A123" "VII SEMIS") ("A143" "VIII SUMMA") ("A163" "IX QUATTUOR"))
(lab-gates "I NON" 11 3 8 1 2)
(lab-gates "II ET" 12 23 8 2 3)
(lab-gates "III VEL" 13 43 8 2 4)
(lab-gates "IV AUT" 14 63 8 2 5)
(lab-gates "V ELIGE" 15 83 8 3 6)
(lab-gates "VI DISTRIBUE" 16 103 8 2 6)
(lab-gates "VII SEMIS" 17 123 8 2 6)
(lab-gates "VIII SUMMA" 18 143 8 3 6)
(lab-gates "IX QUATTUOR" 19 163 9 9 6)

; ---- the Camera: the level N and P move to (docs/SPEC.md section 3.8, version 4's third row) ----
(sheet "Camera" hidden)
(camera 1 1)
(cell "Camera" "A3" "sheet")
(rule "Camera" "B3" Lab!B3)

; ---- the commands (docs/SPEC.md section 3.10): each holds always, and the manifest's (game ...) holds them on the levels ----
(sheet "Commands" hidden)
(headers "Commands" "A1" "name" "words" "holds" "key")
(cells "Commands"
  ("A2" "test")     ("B2" "test the level shown: every input, an input a frame, stopping at the first that fails") ("D2" "KeyT")
  ("A3" "next")     ("B3" "show the next level")                                                                   ("D3" "KeyN")
  ("A4" "previous") ("B4" "show the previous level")                                                               ("D4" "KeyP")
  ("A5" "reset")    ("B5" "set the level's switches to 0, and forget its test")                                    ("D5" "KeyR")
  ("A6" "toggle")   ("B6" "toggle the switch the selection stands on")                                             ("D6" "Space")
  ("A7" "one")      ("B7" "set the switch the selection stands on to 1")                                           ("D7" "Digit1")
  ("A8" "zero")     ("B8" "set the switch the selection stands on to 0")                                           ("D8" "Digit0"))
; ---- the levels' end ----

; ---- the sheet, and its look --------------------------------------------------------------
(sheet "Bench" visible)
(format 1 "E2D8F6" general nowrap)  ; a 1, the lavender family's focus
(look "Bench" 1 1)

